==================================
Analysis of the Hirshfeld atom fit
==================================

An analysis of the fit is deposited in 'stdout.fit_analysis'.

This large file includes:
. A normal QQ plot with each datum labelled by (hkl)
. A plot of F_z = (F_exp-F_pred)/F_sigma vs sin(theta)/lambda :
. A plot of F_z = (F_exp-F_pred)/F_sigma vs F_exp
. A plot of Delta F = (F_exp-F_pred) vs sin(theta)/lambda :

If you used an extinction correction, you also get:
. A plot of (F_pred(no ext)-F_pred(ext))/F_sigma vs. sin (theta/lambda)
. A plot of (F_pred(no ext)-F_pred(ext))/F_sigma vs. F_pred

All of the above plots are available for the reserved (free) data
if you made use of that option. Phew.

Use Excel or gnuplot to view these data. Do it.

